---
title: Owner · started to ready
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> serving : Serve
  state started_at <<choice>>
  serving --> started_at : Started [containers started]
  started_at --> warming : [WaitForReady = FALSE]
  started_at --> starting : [WaitForReady = TRUE]
  state "warming · up returned" as warming
  state "starting · up --wait" as starting
  warming --> ready : Ready [pub = committed]
  starting --> ready : Ready, then up returns
  warming --> failed : Fail (PR C)
  starting --> failed : Fail
  ready --> failed : Fail (PR C)
  warming --> stopped : accept + cancel, DownStop
  ready --> stopped : accept + cancel, DownStop
  starting --> stopped : accept + cancel, DownStop
  stopped --> serving : restart: a new run
  state "failed (PR C)" as failed
  failed --> [*] : retained or recorded
  note right of warming
    up returns here, in order:
    PublishMapping, Bookkeep,
    Notify, OwnerAccept, Return
    INV NoReturnWithoutMapping
    INV NoPrematureReturn
  end note
  note right of stopped
    DownRequest queues the stop,
    even mid-publication. Owner:
    AcceptStop, between passes and
    never mid-publication, cancels
    the wait. Frontend: its own
    FrontendCancel (abort) ends the
    started chain. DownStop needs
    both, in either order.
    INV DownCancelsWait: no Ready
    INV DownHooksOnce: hooks once
    INV NoHalfPublicationAfterStop
    INV StoppedOwnerNotWaiting
    INV StoppedFrontendCancelled
  end note
  note left of starting
    --wait: mapping saved here too;
    bookkeeping and return wait
    for Ready
    INV NoReturnWithoutMapping
  end note
  classDef live stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef idle stroke-width:1.6px
  class serving live
  class warming,starting wait
  class ready ok
  class failed fail
  class stopped idle
